{# The quad the MEMORYLESS sign rule reads on today's axes, or '' when it cannot be
   resolved. `quad` is the sticky hysteresis label and disagreed with this rule on ~44%
   of post-2000 sessions, so a surface that signs "supporting evidence" against the raw
   axes while displaying the sticky label presents evidence AGAINST the call as the
   evidence behind it (engine/regime.flip_condition, fixed 2026-07-29).
   Engine-published first (flip_condition.raw_quad, then run.py's raw_quad); the last
   resort derives it exactly as engine/playbook.quad_meaning_for() does when the column
   is missing, so this can never disagree with the engine's own fallback. Used by every
   surface that has to decide whether the label still has its own axes behind it. #}
{% macro raw_quad_of(latest) -%}
{%- set _fc = (latest.get('flip_condition') or {}) if latest is mapping else {} -%}
{%- set _rq = _fc.get('raw_quad') or (latest.get('raw_quad') if latest is mapping else none) -%}
{%- if _rq in ('Q1', 'Q2', 'Q3', 'Q4') %}{{ _rq }}
{%- else -%}
  {%- set _g = latest.get('growth_score') if latest is mapping else none -%}
  {%- set _i = latest.get('inflation_score') if latest is mapping else none -%}
  {%- if _g is not none and _g is number and _i is not none and _i is number -%}
    {{ ('Q1' if _i < 0 else 'Q2') if _g >= 0 else ('Q4' if _i < 0 else 'Q3') }}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
