    {# ── "What would flip this call" context strip (design-doctrine ruling 2026-07-16).
       Renders ONLY already-calibrated engine keys from data/regime/latest.json:
       flip_condition (weakest supporting component + margin), quad_vector.
       transition_momentum (which quad the model's odds are drifting toward/away
       from), and the top-level label confidence. Conditional framing throughout —
       context, never a forecast; no LLM-originated content. Numbers-with-precision
       (z / threshold / rates) live in the ? help tip (Tier 2); the visible rows
       carry plain words. Emitted in BOTH hero variants (ledger .mx2-hero and grid
       .mx5-sc-left); every key is guarded so an older latest.json skips rows. #}
    {% macro regime_flip_strip(latest) %}
