    {{ pv.pv_css() }}
{#- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    PROPHET LIVE P1 — "Forming today" strip (research/PROPHET_LIVE_P1_DESIGN_SPEC.md).

    ITS OWN panel span12, deliberately NOT a block inside #us-standouts: doctrine Law 4
    allows one as-of stamp per panel and the two clocks here are different objects — the
    board is stamped with the nightly close vintage, this strip with an intraday quote
    age. Two clocks = two panels; merging them would force one stamp to lie.

    PRESENTATION TIER ONLY. Nothing here touches graded-board rows, membership, ordering,
    us_standouts.json or any ledger (DNR §1). The nightly build remains the ONLY confirmer:
    every read on this strip settles at tonight's close and the copy says so in both
    languages. SSR emits the shell only — the panel stays display:none until the JS has a
    payload, so an absent artifact is silence, not an empty box (FT-R8).
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
    {% if mode == 'stocks' %}
    {% set _plv_uni = us_standouts.get('universe') if (us_standouts and us_standouts.get('universe')) else none %}
    <style>
    /* ── PROPHET LIVE strip (P1, spec §3) ─────────────────────────────────────────
       The provisional hue is the lane's OWN component-scoped token, chosen against
       three neighbours — no global token is added and theme.css stays untouched:
         · not --link / --info  → a chip must never read as clickable
         · not --up / --down    → must never read directional (and must not flip under
                                  html[data-lang="zh"] 红涨绿跌)
         · not any --pv-*       → must never read as a nightly verdict (green = confirmed,
                                  and only the nightly build confirms)
       Escalation to the strongest moment (confirming_into_close) is carried by FILL and
       WEIGHT, never by hue: one hue for the whole live family. There is deliberately no
       status dot anywhere — a green "live" pulse is unreachable on a 15-min-delayed plane
       and would encode certainty. The settle rail is the sanctioned proof of life. */
    /* --plv-rh is THE height contract's single free parameter — see .plv-body below. */
    #prophet-live{--plv:#62a0e8;--plv-rh:27px;display:none}
    html[data-theme="light"] #prophet-live{--plv:#2f6fd0}
    #prophet-live.visible{display:block}
    /* Every header item takes the token pill's line box, so a SHORTER token ("READ
       PAUSED") cannot yield a shorter wrapped line than a longer one. Measured: it did,
       by 2.5px — which is a height change, i.e. a board shove. */
    .plv-hd{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;row-gap:4px;flex-wrap:wrap}
    .plv-hd > *{min-height:17px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center}
    /* gap, not a literal space: `.plv-hd > *` makes the title an inline-flex box and flex
       layout discards the whitespace-only text node between the ◐ glyph and the label. */
    .plv-title{margin:0;gap:6px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--plv)}
    .plv-token{font-size:9.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--plv);
      border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--plv) 34%,transparent);
      background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--plv) 9%,transparent);border-radius:999px;padding:1.5px 8px;white-space:nowrap}
    /* ── WORST-CASE RESERVATION (the general fix for mode-dependent height) ──────
       Three boxes here hold text that changes with the MODE, and every one of them was
       an unreserved height variable: a wrapped line count is a function of string
       length, so the panel measured up to 32.75px taller in one mode than another and
       shoved the whole board. Reserving a hand-measured min-height per breakpoint would
       need a magic number per width PER LANGUAGE and would rot the first time a word
       changed. Instead every variant stays in the DOM, stacked in ONE grid cell, and
       only the active one is visible: the browser then reserves max(all modes) at
       whatever width and language it is actually rendering, with no numbers at all.
       `visibility:hidden` is load-bearing — it keeps the box sized while removing the
       inactive text from the accessibility tree, so nothing invisible is ever announced
       or read as a claim. `display:none` would size nothing; `opacity:0` would be read. */
    .plv-hd > .plv-token{display:inline-grid;justify-items:center;text-align:center}
    /* The as-of reserves its line even when it has nothing to stamp: at <=340px it sits on
       header line 2 beside the token, so an empty box collapsed that line and shoved the
       board 17px on exactly the days there is no read to stamp. `tabular-nums` above is
       what makes the 12:00 reserver exactly as wide as any real two-digit-hour stamp. */
    .plv-hd > .plv-asof{display:inline-grid;justify-items:end}
    .plv-sub,.plv-fn{display:grid}
    .plv-v{grid-area:1/1;visibility:hidden}
    .plv-v.is-on{visibility:visible}
    /* The TOKEN only needs a mode-independent width where the header wraps — above the
       680px query it sits on one line with room to spare, so drop the reservation there
       and let the pill hug its own text. Below it the pill keeps a constant width, which
       is what stops a short token ("READ PAUSED") from fitting beside the title where a
       long one wraps and taking the as-of onto a line of its own. */
    @media (min-width:681px){ .plv-token .plv-v:not(.is-on){display:none} }
    .plv-token.is-dark{color:var(--muted);border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 30%,transparent);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--muted) 7%,transparent)}
    .plv-token.is-closed{color:var(--pv-hold);border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-hold) 34%,transparent);background:transparent}
    .plv-more{font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);background:none;border:0;padding:0 2px;font-family:inherit;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px}
    .plv-asof{margin-left:auto;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}
    .plv-sub{font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--text);opacity:.82;margin:5px 0 0;min-height:17px}
    /* SIGNATURE — the settle rail. Fixed height; the only inline style the JS writes
       anywhere on this page is this fill's width (and the now-tick's left). It encodes the
       one variable that actually converts "forming" into "confirmed": remaining tape.
       aria-hidden — the as-of text and the end-cap label carry it in words. */
    .plv-rail{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin:11px 0 10px;height:14px}
    .plv-rail-track{position:relative;flex:1;height:3px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--line);overflow:visible}
    .plv-rail-fill{position:absolute;inset:0 auto 0 0;width:0;height:3px;border-radius:2px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--plv) 46%,transparent)}
    .plv-rail-now{position:absolute;top:-3px;left:0;width:1.5px;height:9px;border-radius:1px;background:var(--plv)}
    .plv-rail-lbl{flex:none;font-size:9.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap}
    #prophet-live.is-dark .plv-rail{opacity:.45}
    #prophet-live.is-dark .plv-rail-fill,#prophet-live.is-dark .plv-rail-now{display:none}
    #prophet-live.is-closed .plv-rail-now{display:none}
    #prophet-live.is-closed .plv-rail-fill{width:100%!important;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-hold) 30%,transparent)}
    /* rows: dtp-column discipline — ONE header labels the figure columns, so no row ever
       repeats a constant (doctrine Law 4) and every figure is self-labelled (Law 3). */
    .plv-cols,.plv-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(96px,auto) 46px 1fr 74px 74px 52px;align-items:baseline;gap:0 10px}
    .plv-cols{font-size:9.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);
      border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding-bottom:4px}
    .plv-c2,.plv-c3,.plv-c4{text-align:right}
    /* EVERY cell is pinned to its column, header and row alike. The labels always were;
       the row cells were auto-placed, and auto-placement RESHUFFLES when a cell in the
       middle is removed: the ≤560px rule hides .plv-nm (column 3), so `now` slid into
       that column — which the same rule sets to 0 — and printed on top of `cross level`
       ("$224260.85" at 375px). Pinning makes any future column demotion a no-op for the
       cells that stay. */
    .plv-c1{grid-column:1}.plv-c2{grid-column:4}.plv-c3{grid-column:5}.plv-c4{grid-column:6}
    .plv-row > .plv-chip{grid-column:1}
    .plv-tk{grid-column:2}.plv-nm{grid-column:3}
    .plv-now{grid-column:4}.plv-lvl{grid-column:5}.plv-since{grid-column:6}
    /* empty modes keep the hairline rule (height invariance) but HIDE rather than collapse
       the labels — dead column headings over an empty box read as a broken panel. */
    #prophet-live.is-empty .plv-cols > span{visibility:hidden}
    /* THE HEIGHT CONTRACT — 3 reserved slots, and the reservation is DERIVED from the row
       height instead of being a second hand-measured number. The spec (and the mockup)
       pinned both sides independently at min-height 24.5px / 75.5px; on the real page the
       row measures 26.06px, because this page inherits line-height:1.5 while the mockup
       inherited `normal`, and a baseline-aligned grid row is as tall as
       max(above-baseline) + max(below-baseline) across the chip and the text — not as tall
       as the chip box. The strip came out 4.69px taller in live than in quiet/dark/closed:
       a board shove every time the last cross faded. Two independently guessed numbers
       cannot stay equal, so now `height` (not min-height) fixes the row and the body
       reserves exactly 3 of them. --plv-rh is the one parameter; it must stay >= the row's
       natural content height (21.06px content + 5px padding at time of writing). Re-run
       mockups/refs/prophet_live/verify_p1.py after ANY change to the chip box, the row
       font sizes, or the inherited line-height. */
    .plv-body{min-height:calc(var(--plv-rh) * 3 + 2px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:2px}
    .plv-row{padding:2.5px 0;height:var(--plv-rh);box-sizing:border-box;font-size:12.5px;text-decoration:none;color:inherit}
    .plv-row:hover .plv-nm,.plv-row:hover .plv-tk{color:var(--link)}
    .plv-tk{font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.01em;white-space:nowrap}
    .plv-nm{color:var(--muted);font-size:11px;min-width:0;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}
    .plv-now,.plv-lvl,.plv-since{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-family:var(--font-mono,monospace);white-space:nowrap}
    .plv-now{font-weight:700}
    .plv-lvl{color:var(--muted)}
    .plv-since{color:var(--muted);font-size:11px}
    .plv-chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;justify-self:start;font-size:10px;font-weight:800;
      letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:1.35;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;white-space:nowrap;
      background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--plv) 10%,transparent);color:var(--plv);
      border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--plv) 42%,transparent)}
    /* the strongest moment escalates by FILL + WEIGHT, never by hue */
    .plv-chip--close{background:var(--plv);color:#fff;border-color:transparent}
    /* "fell back" (grey, it came back toward you) vs "ran past" (amber, don't chase) —
       the two fade stories never share a word and never share a hue, and neither uses a
       directional colour, so 红涨绿跌 holds by construction. Do not add --up/--down. */
    .plv-chip--drop{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-hold) 10%,transparent);color:var(--pv-hold);
      border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-hold) 32%,transparent)}
    .plv-chip--over{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-wait) 11%,transparent);color:var(--pv-wait);
      border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pv-wait) 40%,transparent)}
    .plv-row.is-past .plv-tk,.plv-row.is-past .plv-now{opacity:.72}
    .plv-none{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:3px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}
    .plv-last{font-size:10.5px;opacity:.8}
    .plv-fn{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:7px;padding-top:7px;font-size:10.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted)}
    .plv-fig{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-weight:700;color:var(--text)}  /* figures mono, words never */
    .plv-row.is-new{animation:plv-in .2s ease-out}
    @keyframes plv-in{from{opacity:0}to{opacity:1}}
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.plv-row.is-new{animation:none}}
    @media (max-width:680px){
      /* Header pinned to a deterministic TWO lines: [title ? +N] / [token as-of].
         The reorder alone is not enough. Without it the 44px +N button landed on a THIRD
         line the moment a 4th row appeared — a 21px shove of the whole board, every 5
         minutes. With it, WHICH line the token lands on was still a function of its own
         string length: the short "READ PAUSED" fitted beside the title while
         "INTRADAY · 15-MIN DELAYED" did not, so the header measured 40.25px in dark
         against 41.25px in live — a 1px shove on every mode change. The ::before is a
         zero-content flex item with basis 100%: it consumes the rest of line 1, so the
         token ALWAYS starts line 2 no matter how long it is, and it carries the 4px the
         row-gap gave up so the pinned height is unchanged (18 + 4 + 19.25). */
      .plv-hd{row-gap:0}
      .plv-hd::before{content:"";order:2;flex:0 0 100%;height:4px}
      .plv-more{order:1;margin-left:auto}
      .plv-token{order:3}
      .plv-asof{order:4;margin-left:auto}
      .plv-cols,.plv-row{grid-template-columns:minmax(84px,auto) 44px 1fr 68px 68px 0}
      .plv-c4,.plv-since{display:none}          /* SINCE demoted; it survives in the row tip */
    }
    @media (max-width:560px){
      /* Phone layout: [chip] [ticker] · [now]. Two things had to change here.
         (1) Column 1 keeps min-content. With minmax(0,auto) the grid handed column 1 ZERO
             pixels — the 1fr name column outbid it — and the 148px "HOLDING INTO CLOSE"
             pill printed straight over the ticker at 375px and below.
         (2) The chip is then allowed to WRAP rather than to shorten. Collapsing it to the
             bare ◐ glyph (the card-chip idiom) would leave hue as the only carrier of the
             state, and on the strip the state word IS the content. Wrapping costs row
             height instead — paid ONCE through --plv-rh, so every mode grows together and
             the height contract still holds.
         Cross level is demoted here with the company name (both survive in the row tip);
         NOW stays, because it is the figure the reader is actually looking for. .plv-c3 is
         the CROSS LEVEL heading (column 5), so it goes with .plv-lvl — not with .plv-nm,
         which has no heading of its own. */
      #prophet-live{--plv-rh:40px}
      .plv-cols,.plv-row{grid-template-columns:minmax(min-content,auto) 44px minmax(0,1fr) 66px 0 0;
        gap:0 8px;align-items:center}
      .plv-nm,.plv-c3,.plv-lvl{display:none}
      .plv-chip{white-space:normal;text-align:center}
    }
    </style>
    <div class="panel span12" id="prophet-live" hidden{% if _plv_uni %} data-universe="{{ _plv_uni }}"{% endif %}>
      <div class="plv-hd">
        <h2 class="plv-title">◐ {{ t('Forming today', '今日正在形成') }}</h2>
        {#- The Tier-2 receipt (spec §4.6). Tip text is [js]-written and then handed to
            theme.js's upgradeHelpIcons() for the shared tap-to-toggle popover: the
            sentence carries the intraday coverage count, which changes every pass, so
            baking it here would ship a stale receipt. Empty spans keep upgradeOne() from
            freezing a placeholder into data-tip-en before the fill. #}
        <span class="help" id="plv-help">?<span class="tip tip-wide"><span class="l-en"></span><span class="l-zh"></span></span></span>
        <span class="plv-token" id="plv-token"></span>
        <button class="plv-more" id="plv-more" type="button" aria-expanded="false" hidden></button>
        <span class="plv-asof" id="plv-asof"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="plv-sub" id="plv-sub"></div>
      <div class="plv-rail" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="plv-rail-track"><i class="plv-rail-fill" id="plv-rail-fill"></i><i class="plv-rail-now" id="plv-rail-now"></i></div>
        <div class="plv-rail-lbl">{{ t('settles 4:00 pm ET', '美东 16:00 结算') }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="plv-cols" id="plv-cols">
        <span class="plv-c1"></span>
        <span class="plv-c2">{{ t('Now', '当前') }}</span>
        <span class="plv-c3">{{ t('Cross level', '上穿价位') }}</span>
        <span class="plv-c4">{{ t('Since', '起始') }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="plv-body" id="plv-body"></div>
      <div class="plv-fn" id="plv-fn"></div>
    </div>
    {#- ticker → company name for the strip rows. The prophet_live payload carries no
        names, and the names it needs are by construction NOT on the board below (a
        strip row is a name that crossed TODAY and was not admitted last night), so
        the cards cannot supply them. This island is the near-decision population the
        pack arms from — buy ∪ watch ∪ leaders ∪ laggards, ~150 short strings — which
        costs one baked object instead of a second network fetch. DISPLAY-ONLY: a
        label lookup, never a membership or ordering input. #}
    {%- set _plv_nm = {} -%}
    {%- if us_standouts -%}
      {%- for _lst in ['watch', 'buy', 'leaders', 'laggards'] -%}
        {%- for _r in (us_standouts.get(_lst) or []) -%}
          {%- if _r.get('ticker') and _r.get('name') -%}{{ _plv_nm.update({_r.ticker: _r.name}) or '' }}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif %}
    <script type="application/json" id="plv-names">{{ _plv_nm | tojson }}</script>
    {% endif %}
    {% if _su or action_board.notable %}
    <div class="panel span12 notable" id="us-standouts">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <h2 style="margin:0">{{ t('Prophet Stock Signals', '先知选股') }}</h2>
        {# W8-R6: grid/table view toggle (US market) #}
        {% if _su %}
        <span class="st-view-toggle" id="us-st-view-toggle" role="group" data-tip-en="Switch between grid and table view" data-tip-zh="切换卡片视图与表格视图">
          <button id="us-st-btn-grid" aria-selected="true" onclick="USStockTable._setView('grid')">&#8862; <span class="l-en">Grid</span><span class="l-zh">卡片</span></button>
          <button id="us-st-btn-table" aria-selected="false" onclick="USStockTable._setView('table')">&#9776; <span class="l-en">Table</span><span class="l-zh">表格</span></button>
        </span>
        {% endif %}
        {% if _su %}{% set _su_delayed = (_su.get('staleness') or {}).get('delayed') %}<span class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px">{{ _su.buy|length }} {{ t("shown ·", "已显示 ·") }} {{ _su.eligible }} {% if _su_delayed %}{{ t("setups · dots reflect prices as of " ~ ((_su.staleness or {}).get('price_through') or '?') ~ " — verify before acting.", "个形态 · 价格点位截至 " ~ ((_su.staleness or {}).get('price_through') or '?') ~ "，操作前请确认最新价格。") }}{% else %}{{ t("setups · green dot = entry open, yellow = wait for pullback.", "个形态 · 绿点＝现在可入场，黄点＝等回调。") }}{% endif %}
          <span class="help">?<span class="tip tip-wide">{% if _su_delayed %}<span class="l-en">Board is delayed — prices are as of {{ ((_su.staleness or {}).get('price_through') or '?') }}. Dots and entry signals may not reflect current prices. Conviction: is this a name worth owning? Entry: verify current price before acting. Click a card for the full breakdown.</span><span class="l-zh">数据延迟 — 价格截至 {{ ((_su.staleness or {}).get('price_through') or '?') }}。绿点及入场信号可能不反映最新价格。信念：是否值得持有；入场：操作前请确认当前价格。点击卡片查看完整拆解。</span>{% else %}<span class="l-en">Each card answers two separate questions. Conviction: is this a name worth owning? Entry: is today a good price? High conviction can still mean wait for the pullback. Green dot = entry open · yellow = wait · the alpha chip ranks selection edge. Click a card for the full breakdown.</span><span class="l-zh">每张卡片回答两个独立问题。信念：是否值得持有；入场：今天价格是否合适。高信念也可能需要等回调。绿点＝入场窗口已开 · 黄点＝等待 · alpha 标记为选股优势排名。点击卡片看完整拆解。</span>{% endif %}</span></span></span>{% endif %}
        {% if not _su %}<span class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px">{{ t("Top-10 holdings per sector · grouped by cycle entry, ranked by alpha.", "各板块前十大持仓 · 按周期入场分组，以alpha排序。") }}
          {{ help("Every sector ETF’s top-10 holdings are run through the SAME price-cycle engine as the sectors. A name earns a card only when its cycle signal is decisive — a confirmed buy (BUY ZONE), an imminent turn (BOTTOMING), or a sell (TOPPING). The cycle state GROUPS the cards (it places risk — a defined entry + exit); WITHIN each group they’re ordered by the validated sector-neutral residual momentum (α — market + sector beta stripped). We Phase-0 tested blending the cycle timing INTO the rank (reports/setup-score-phase0.md, survivorship-clean S&P 500, 12y) and it did NOT improve forward returns — it diluted α — so the order rides α and the cycle/pullback is shown as risk-placement CONTEXT, not a return signal. A soft per-sector cap keeps one hot sector from crowding the board. The α / #rank / pullback line and the 👤 insider chip are context inputs, NOT standalone buy signals. Click any card for the full breakdown.", "每个板块 ETF 的前十大持仓都用与板块相同的价格周期引擎分析。只有当个股的周期信号具决定性时才会获得卡片 — 已确认买入（买入区）、即将转向（筑底）或卖出（做顶）。周期状态对卡片进行分组（它摆放风险 — 明确的入场与出场）；在每组内部，按已验证的行业中性残差动量（α — 已剥离大盘与行业 beta）排序。我们做了 Phase-0 检验，把周期择时混入排序（reports/setup-score-phase0.md，无幸存者偏差的标普500，12年），结果并未改善前瞻收益 — 反而稀释了 α — 因此排序以 α 为准，周期/回调作为风险摆位的情境展示，而非收益信号。软性的单一板块上限可避免强势板块挤占整版。卡片上的 α / #排名 / 回调一行以及 👤 内部人买入标记均为情境输入，并非独立买入信号。点击任意卡片查看完整拆解。") }}</span>{% endif %}
      </div>
      {# market dealer-gamma context banner removed by operator request 2026-07-11 —
         the market_gamma vm key and engine.market_gamma stay (gex board still uses them). #}
      {# G6a donor-sector context chip — market-wide rotation state, US only (display-only).
         Rendered only when the donor object exists in us_standouts (set by build_stock_library).
         'cracking' = fresh weekly RSI-MACD bearish cross on the top-126d-EW-return GICS sector
         composite within the trailing 4 completed weeks, OR its 20d return < 0.
         'intact' = neither leg fires. NOT a trade signal — context for entry sizing. #}
      {% if _su and _su.donor and _su.donor.donor_sector %}{% set _don = _su.donor %}
      <div class="nb-donor donor-{{ _don.state }}" data-tip-en="{{ 'Rotation: the leading GICS sector (' + _don.donor_sector + ', top-126d equal-weight return across ' + (_don.n_sectors | string) + ' sectors) shows signs of cracking — a fresh weekly RSI-MACD bearish cross on its composite within the last 4 completed weeks, or its 20-day EW return has gone negative. Historically, stock entries during donor cracking have higher clean-exit rates (G6a, +5.96 pp deep / +5.81 pp baskets, episode LB +2.66 pp). DISPLAY-ONLY: does not change rankings, gates, or sizing. Context for your own entry-timing discipline.' if _don.state == 'cracking' else 'Rotation: the leading GICS sector (' + _don.donor_sector + ', top-126d equal-weight return across ' + (_don.n_sectors | string) + ' sectors) is intact — no fresh weekly RSI-MACD bearish cross in the last 4 completed weeks and its 20-day EW return is positive. The rotation leader is still running. DISPLAY-ONLY: context only, not a signal.' }} · {{ _don.state }} · {{ _don.donor_sector }} · as of {{ _don.asof }}" data-tip-zh="{{ '轮动：领涨GICS板块（' + _don.donor_sector + '，全市场126日等权收益最高，共' + (_don.n_sectors | string) + '个板块）显现趋弱迹象——过去4个已完结周内出现周线RSI-MACD看跌交叉，或其20日等权收益已转负。历史数据显示，领涨板块趋弱期间入场的胜率更高（G6a，深度+5.96pp / 篮子+5.81pp）。仅供参考：不影响排名、门控或仓位。' if _don.state == 'cracking' else '轮动：领涨GICS板块（' + _don.donor_sector + '，全市场126日等权收益最高，共' + (_don.n_sectors | string) + '个板块）运行稳健——过去4个已完结周内无周线RSI-MACD看跌交叉，且20日等权收益为正。轮动领涨板块仍在运行。仅供参考：非交易信号。' }} · {{ _don.state }} · {{ _don.donor_sector }} · as of {{ _don.asof }}">
        <span class="donor-ic">{{ '⟳' if _don.state == 'cracking' else '✓' }}</span>
        <b><span class="l-en">Rotation: </span><span class="l-zh">轮动：</span>{{ td(_don.donor_sector) }}{% if _don.state == 'cracking' %}<span class="l-en"> — the 6-month sector leader is cooling. Historically a decent window to start new positions, not a sell signal.</span><span class="l-zh"> — 半年领涨板块正在降温。历史上是开新仓的尚可窗口，而非卖出信号。</span>{% else %}<span class="l-en"> — the 6-month sector leader, still running strong.</span><span class="l-zh"> — 半年领涨板块，依然强势。</span>{% endif %}</b>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {# W1.5 earnings-blackout: suppressed-today compact note.
         Shown only when 1+ fresh-buy candidates were suppressed today (store must be fresh).
         The note names the suppressed tickers so the user can look them up manually.
         Bilingual via l-en/l-zh spans; no translated text in attributes (check_title_i18n). #}
      {% if _su and _su.get('earnings_blackout_note') %}
      {% set _ebn = _su.earnings_blackout_note %}
      {% if _ebn.count %}
      <div class="nb-eb-note"
        data-tip-en="W1.5 earnings-blackout hygiene (adjudicated 2026-07-05): fresh entries within 3 trading days of an earnings date are suppressed from this board. The setup signal itself is unchanged — you can review these names on their stock detail pages."
        data-tip-zh="W1.5 财报屏蔽规则（2026-07-05裁定）：财报前3个交易日内的新鲜入场信号不出现在本榜单。形态信号本身未变——可在各股票详情页查看这些标的。"
      ><span class="l-en">📅 {{ _ebn.count }} setup{{ 's' if _ebn.count != 1 else '' }} suppressed today (earnings ≤3d): {{ _ebn.tickers | join(', ') }}</span><span class="l-zh">📅 今日{{ _ebn.count }}个形态因财报（≤3天）被屏蔽：{{ _ebn.tickers | join(', ') }}</span></div>
      {% endif %}
      {% endif %}
      {# CSP-W5 board staleness badge — shown when the underlying ohlcv store is
         >= 2 trading sessions behind the expected NYSE session.  Fail-soft: absent
         key or delayed=False = nothing shown.  Bilingual via l-en/l-zh spans;
         no translated text in attributes (check_title_i18n). #}
      {% if _su and _su.get('staleness') and _su.staleness.get('delayed') %}
      {% set _stale = _su.staleness %}
      <div class="nb-stale-note">
        <span class="l-en">⚠ BOARD DELAYED — priced {{ _stale.get('price_through', '?') }} ({{ _stale.get('age_days', '?') }}d behind). Data is stale; entries shown may not reflect latest prices.</span><span class="l-zh">⚠ 数据延迟 — 价格截至 {{ _stale.get('price_through', '?') }}（落后 {{ _stale.get('age_days', '?') }} 天）。当前数据过期，入场信号可能不反映最新价格。</span>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {# B4 Conviction Delta — data prep for the "What changed today" dashboard.
         Rendered only when us_standouts.delta exists and has >=1 entry.
         Purely descriptive: shows which verb and which reason-codes changed.
         No advice verbs, no causal phrasing. Fail-soft: absent key = no button. #}
      {% set _has_delta = _su and _su.get('delta') and _su.delta.get('entries') %}
      {% if _has_delta %}
      {% set _dlt = _su.delta %}
      {% set _NBR_EN = {'freshness_expired':'Cross too old — wait for a fresh trigger','not_topped':'Topped / overbought — wait for it to reset','earnings_blackout':'Earnings within blackout window','risk_veto':'Stressed tape — size down or wait','extended':'Extended / parabolic — do not chase','capped_by_entry':'Entry capped — entry timing blocks a full buy'} %}
      {% set _NBR_ZH = {'freshness_expired':'交叉信号过期——等待新触发','not_topped':'超买/见顶——等待重置','earnings_blackout':'处于财报窗口期','risk_veto':'盘面承压——减仓或等待','extended':'过度拉伸/抛物线——勿追高','capped_by_entry':'入场封顶——入场时机阻碍满仓'} %}
      {% endif %}
      {# ── W8-R6: US stocktable JSON data block + mount points ───────────
         Serializes us_standouts.buy rows with flat keys for StockTable.init.
         No re-ordering: system order is preserved (CN no-mutation pattern).
         Rendered only when us_standouts.buy is populated (mode=stocks only). #}
      {% if _su %}
      <script type="application/json" id="us-stocktable-data">
      {
        "rows": [{% for _n in _su.buy %}{% if not loop.first %},{% endif %}{
          "ticker":        {{ _n.ticker | tojson }},
          "name":          {{ _n.name | tojson }},
          "sector":        {{ (_n.sector or '') | tojson }},
          "lane":          {{ (_n.get('lane') or '') | tojson }},
          "stage":         {{ ({'bottoming':'ENTRY','continuation':'ENTRY','trend':'ENTRY','recovery':'RIPENING','watch':'RAN_LATE'}.get(_n.get('lane') or 'watch', 'ENTRY')) | tojson }},
          "price":         {{ _n.get('price') | tojson }},
          "conviction_score": {{ ((_n.conviction or {}).get('score')) | tojson }},
          "alpha":         {{ _n.get('alpha') | tojson }},
          "off_high":      {{ _n.get('off_high') | tojson }},
          "factor_z":      {{ _n.get('factor_z') | tojson }},
          "sue_z":         {{ _n.get('sue_z') | tojson }},
          "insider_buyers": {{ _n.get('insider_buyers') | tojson }},
          "sig_tier":      {{ ((_n.signal or {}).get('tier_cascade') or '') | tojson }},
          "entry_status":  {{ ((_n.entry_signal or {}).get('status') or '') | tojson }},
          "dir":           {{ (_n.get('dir') or '') | tojson }}
        }{% endfor %}],
        "as_of": {{ (_su.get('as_of') or '') | tojson }}
      }
      </script>
      {# ── count chips (id must match the hard-coded id in stocktable.js line 376) ── #}
      <div id="st-count-chips" style="display:none"></div>
      {# ── table view mount point ── #}
      <div id="us-stocktable-wrap"></div>
      {% endif %}
      {# ── grid section (hidden in table mode via CSS) ── #}
      <div class="nb-grid-section">
      <div class="nbgrid" data-showmore-rows="3">
      {% if _su %}
      {# CONFLUENCE-GATED board (2026-07-16): shows names whose signal_gate T1->T4
         cascade verdict is eligible (parity with CN/HK), ordered by the weighted
         cascade blend then alpha-desc within lane (W8). Bottoming-alignment survives
         as per-card context (align_tier badge + lane derivation). Order is set by the
         JSON producer (build_stock_library.py rank_by="confluence"); the template
         renders as-is — no re-sort here. #}
      {% set _board = _su.buy %}
      {# ⚡ PRESENTATION MERGE (2026-07-24 masterplan, research/PROPHET_TOPSETUPS_
         PRESENTATION_MERGE_MASTERPLAN.md): membership in the Top-setups artifact IS
         the fresh-trigger gate — never re-derive freshness from row.signal here
         (the artifact carries signal_gate.is_buyable; a local re-derivation drifts).
         Map ticker -> setups row so the card chip can read the tier; the sub-board
         below reuses the carded-ticker set to list only residual (non-carded) names.
         Fail-soft: top_setups absent/None -> empty map -> no chips, board unchanged. #}
      {%- set _trg_map = {} -%}
      {%- if top_setups and top_setups.buy is defined and top_setups.buy -%}
        {%- for _tr in top_setups.buy -%}{%- if _tr.get('ticker') -%}{%- set _ = _trg_map.update({_tr.ticker: _tr}) -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {# --- TRUE STABLE LANE PARTITION (P2.4 §4.2).
           Canonical group order: bottoming, continuation, trend, recovery, watch (skip empty).
           Cards with lane missing/None render FIRST, ungrouped, with NO heading (honest
           degradation — dev VM with lane=None exercises this path).
           Within each lane group, producer order is preserved (stable selectattr filter).
           Sub-heading shows label · count (l-en/l-zh); per-card left-border accents kept. --- #}
      {%- set _lane_order = ['bottoming','continuation','trend','recovery','watch'] -%}
      {%- set _lane_labels_en = {'bottoming':'Bottoming','continuation':'Continuation','trend':'Trend','recovery':'Recovery','watch':'Watch'} -%}
      {%- set _lane_labels_zh = {'bottoming':'筑底','continuation':'延续','trend':'趋势','recovery':'复苏','watch':'观察'} -%}
      {%- set _render_list = namespace(items=[]) -%}
      {# 1. ungrouped cards first (lane absent or None) — no heading #}
      {%- for _n in _board -%}
        {%- if not _n.get('lane') -%}{%- set _render_list.items = _render_list.items + [_n] -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {# 2. canonical lane groups — heading sentinel then group cards #}
      {%- for _lk in _lane_order -%}
        {%- set _grp = _board | selectattr('lane', 'equalto', _lk) | list -%}
        {%- if _grp -%}
          {%- set _render_list.items = _render_list.items + [{'_heading': true, 'lane': _lk, 'count': _grp|length}] + _grp -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {# 3. CATCH-ALL: cards whose lane is truthy but not in the canonical list (e.g. a future
            lane value shipped by the engine before the template is updated). Rendered ungrouped
            (no heading) at the end so no card is ever silently dropped. Guarantees that a new
            engine-emitted lane value degrades gracefully to "visible but unlabelled" rather than
            disappearing entirely. None-lane cards are already handled in step 1 above. #}
      {%- for _n in _board -%}
        {%- if _n.get('lane') and _n.get('lane') not in _lane_order -%}
          {%- set _render_list.items = _render_list.items + [_n] -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {% for n in _render_list.items %}
        {# heading sentinel: emit featherweight lane sub-heading and skip card rendering #}
        {% if n.get('_heading') %}
        <div class="nb-lane-hd">
          <span class="l-en">{{ _lane_labels_en.get(n.lane, n.lane) }} · {{ n.count }}</span>
          <span class="l-zh">{{ _lane_labels_zh.get(n.lane, n.lane) }} · {{ n.count }}</span>
        </div>
        {% else %}
        {# ═══ PROPHET CARD (flagship redesign, operator-ratified 2026-07-21) ═══
           The old multi-chip standout card is retired; every prior at-rest disclosure
           survives DEMOTED, not deleted: verdict sentence + entry headline → verb-chip
           tooltip; cautions / sector-stance / anti-chase / extension / earnings-window /
           base-broken → the single ⚠N popover; Edge %ile meaning → Edge tooltip; tier/sig
           badge + cycle detail → stock.html analyzer (one click). Builder fields consumed
           unchanged — display-tier change only; lane grouping (R7) untouched. #}
        {% set c = n.conviction %}
        {% set es = n.entry_signal %}
        {% set _is_triage = (c and c.get('score_edge') is not none and c.score_edge >= 80) and (es and es.get('status') in ['buy_now','partial']) %}
        {% set _st = es.status if es else none %}
        {% set _verb = 'buy' if _st in ('buy_now','partial')
                 else ('near' if _st in ('buy_soon','await_confluence')
                 else ('hold' if _st in ('hold','topping')
                 else ('avoid' if _st in ('exit','avoid')
                 else ('wait' if _st
                 else ('near' if n.dir == 'up' else ('avoid' if n.dir == 'down' else 'wait')))))) %}
        {% set _stage = {'bottoming':1,'recovery':2,'continuation':3,'trend':4}.get(n.get('lane') or '', 0) %}
        {% set _vs = c.vol_squeeze if c else none %}
        {% set _vs_fired = _vs and _vs.state in ['FIRED_UP','EXPANSION'] %}
        {% set _entry_ok = not (es and es.get('status') in ['extended','topping','exit','avoid','blocked']) %}
        {% set _fl = namespace(rows=[]) %}
        {% if c %}{% for cau in (c.cautions or []) %}{% if cau != 'accounting watch' %}{% set _z = c.cautions_zh[loop.index0] if (c.cautions_zh and c.cautions_zh|length > loop.index0) else cau %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [(cau, _z)] %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
        {% if (_vs_fired or n.get('alpha_entry') == 'extended') and _entry_ok %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [("Already moving. Don't chase above the buy zone.", '已在异动。不要在买区上方追高。')] %}{% endif %}
        {% if n.get('ext_z') is not none and n.ext_z > 2.0 %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [('Stretched unusually far above its trend line, so chasing is risky.', '远高于趋势线，追高风险较大。')] %}{% endif %}
        {% if n.get('antichase_shadow_blocked') %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [('Parabolic tail. Treat any entry here as a chase.', '处于抛物线尾部。此处入场应视同追高。')] %}{% endif %}
        {% set _es_chip = n.get('earnings_soon') %}
        {% if _es_chip and _es_chip.get('days_to') is not none %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [(_es_chip.get('chip_en') or ('Earnings in ' ~ _es_chip.days_to ~ 'd'), _es_chip.get('chip_zh') or ('财报还有' ~ _es_chip.days_to ~ '天'))] %}{% endif %}
        {% if n.get('sector_stance') and n.sector_stance in ('Reduce','Cautious') %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [('Sector stance is ' ~ n.sector_stance|lower ~ '. This is a single-stock trigger, not a sector call.', '板块态度为' ~ (n.sector_stance_zh or n.sector_stance) ~ '。个股信号，非板块判断。')] %}{% endif %}
        {% if n.get('hold') and n.hold.get('state') == 'broken' %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [('Base broken: price hit the level that voids the thesis.', '筑底破位：价格已触及使论点失效的水平。')] %}{% endif %}
        {# OEU M-PRO: display-tier options context, folded into the SAME ⚠ popover as every
           other caution (no new chip, no layout change). Rows are pre-derived (en, zh) pairs
           attached by build_site._attach_board_display_chips via lib/options_context.py; the
           fence lives there — nothing here touches verb, stage, zone or edge. Names without
           options coverage carry no key and the card renders exactly as before. #}
        {% for _o in (n.get('options_flags') or []) %}{% set _fl.rows = _fl.rows + [(_o[0], _o[1])] %}{% endfor %}
        {% set _bz = es.buy_zone if es else none %}
        {% set _zk = ('readd' if _verb == 'hold' else ('active' if _verb in ('buy','near') else 'muted')) if (_bz and _bz.high is not none) else ('confirm' if _verb in ('wait','near') else 'none') %}
        {% set _tip_en = ((c.verdict if c else '') ~ (' · ' if (c and es) else '') ~ (es.headline if es else '')) %}
        {% set _tip_zh = ((c.verdict_zh if c else '') ~ (' · ' if (c and es) else '') ~ (es.headline_zh if es else '')) %}
        {# ⚡ fresh-trigger chip: kind from the setups row's own signal tier (T3 = imminent,
           else fired). Tips are plain strings (attribute-safe — no t() in attrs). The verb
           stays the ruling stance; the tip says so for the Wait+⚡ case. #}
        {% set _tsr = _trg_map.get(n.ticker) %}
        {% set _tsg = (_tsr.get('signal') or {}) if _tsr else {} %}
        {% set _trg_kind = ('imminent' if _tsg.get('tier_cascade') == 'T3' else 'fired') if _tsr else none %}
        {% set _trg_prov = ' Provisional: projected off an incomplete bar — about 1 in 10 of these vanish when the bar completes.' if (_trg_kind == 'imminent' and _tsg.get('provisional')) else '' %}
        {% set _trg_prov_zh = '（暂定：基于未完成的K线推算 — 约十分之一会在K线完成后消失。）' if (_trg_kind == 'imminent' and _tsg.get('provisional')) else '' %}
        {% set _trg_tip_en = ('Fresh entry trigger — the 2-day MACD and 3-day StochRSI both crossed up within the last ~6 days and momentum is still constructive. A conviction card plus a fresh trigger is the strongest read on this board — but the main chip still rules: if this card says Wait, price has already run past the zone; don\'t chase.') if _trg_kind == 'fired' else ('Entry trigger imminent — the 3-day StochRSI has crossed and the 2-day MACD is about to cross within the next 1-2 bars.' ~ _trg_prov ~ ' The main chip still rules the stance.') %}
